<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/037Y">Remark <span data-tag="037Y">4.5.3.26</span>.</a> In the situation of Corollary <a data-tag="02VM" href="/tag/02VM">4.5.3.24</a>, it is not necessary to assume that $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is an $\infty $-category: every morphism of simplicial sets $f: X \rightarrow Z$ admits a factorization $X \xrightarrow {f'} Y \xrightarrow {f''} Z$, where $f''$ is an isofibration and $f'$ both a monomorphism and a categorical equivalence (Proposition <a class="" data-content="This is a reference to something which is not yet available in Kerodon." data-html="true" data-placement="bottom" data-toggle="popover" data-trigger="focus" role="button" style="cursor: pointer;" tabindex="0" title="Future reference"><img src="/static/images/question.svg"/></a>). However, the proof is somewhat more difficult. </p>
